Fix: put logging and side effects inside `step.run`, which executes once and is memoized.

```ts
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  const ms = await step.run(`pick-delay-${i}`, () => {
    console.log(`iteration ${i}`); // logs once
    return Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000) + 1000;
  });
  await step.sleep(`sleep-${i}`, ms);
  await step.run(`work-${i}`, () => {
    console.log(`work ${i}`);
  });
}
```

If you want to keep logs outside steps without duplicates, use the `logger` passed to the handler, which is designed to dedupe across replays.

